 Set `NODE_NAME` and `NODE_SOLANA_ADDRESS` in `wrangler.toml` or as dashboard
 environment variables for the health response.
 
+## Second Relay Federation
+
+ForkMesh can run a second relay as a federated Worker deployment.
+The main relay is the deployment with no `MAIN_RELAY_URL`.
+A federated relay sets `MAIN_RELAY_URL=https://forkmesh.com`, keeps its own D1 database and Durable Objects, and signs relay-to-main calls with an auto-generated Ed25519 identity stored in `relay_self`.
+Signup custody stays on the main relay, so the federated relay stores only the returned deposit address and federation reference.
+
+Create a separate D1 database for the second relay:
+
+```sh
+uvx --from workers-py pywrangler d1 create forkmesh-yourname
+```
+
+Copy `.env.production.example` to `.env.production` and fill the second-relay settings:
+
+```sh
+FORKMESH_WORKER_NAME=forkmesh-relay-yourname
+FORKMESH_D1_NAME=forkmesh-yourname
+FORKMESH_D1_DATABASE_ID=your-second-relay-d1-database-id
+MAIN_RELAY_URL=https://forkmesh.com
+RELAY_LABEL=your-relay-label
+PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://your-relay.example
+```
+
+Keep `FORKMESH_D1_DATABASE_ID` distinct from the committed primary D1 id.
+`deploy.sh` fails early when `MAIN_RELAY_URL` is set but the Worker name or D1 target still points at the primary relay.
+`TREASURY_SOLANA_ADDRESS` is required on the main relay.
+It is optional on a federated relay because treasury lookup and signup custody proxy through the main relay.
+
+Validate and deploy the federated relay:
+
+```sh
+./deploy.sh dry-run
+./deploy.sh deploy
+```
+
+After deployment, check health:
+
+```sh
+curl -s https://your-relay.example/health
+```
+
+The response should include `"relayRole":"federated"` and a `federation` object.
+Cron registers the relay with the main relay at `/api/federation/register`.
+Until approval, the main relay records it as `pending` and rejects custody or node-presence reports with `relay_not_approved`.
+
+Approve the relay on the main relay with either a direct D1 update:
+
+```sql
+UPDATE relays SET status = 'approved' WHERE label = 'your-relay-label';
+```
+
+or the signed admin API `/api/accounts/admin-relay-approve`.
+After approval, point the Qt client's relay switcher at the second relay host.
+Verify that the client connects, signup payment proxying works, account finalization completes locally, heartbeats continue, and the main relay network payout view includes approved federated presence.
+
+This MVP does not merge catalogs across relays, bridge chat rooms across relays, add automatic relay discovery, or add WebRTC routing.
+
